text: ['({B/R} can be paid with either {B} or {R}.)\\nEnchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/-1.', '({B/R} can be paid with either {B} or {R}.)\\nFlying\\nWhen Avatar of Discord enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you discard two cards.', '({B/R} can be paid with either {B} or {R}.)\\n{3}{B}, Discard a card: Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.\\n{3}{R}: Create a 2/1 red Goblin creature token with haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step.', "({R/G} can be paid with either {R} or {G}.)\\nTrample; haste; shroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", '({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', '({W/B} can be paid with either {W} or {B}.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control.', "({W/U} can be paid with either {W} or {U}.)\\nWhenever a player casts a noncreature spell, counter that spell. That player creates X 1/1 white and blue Bird creature tokens with flying, where X is the spell's mana value.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, Rumbling Slum deals 1 damage to each player.', "Azorius Chancery enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Azorius Chancery enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {W}{U}.", "Azorius Herald can't be blocked.\\nWhen Azorius Herald enters the battlefield, you gain 4 life.\\nWhen Azorius Herald enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless {U} was spent to cast it.", 'Bloodrush — {1}{R}{G}, Discard Zhur-Taa Swine: Target attacking creature gets +5/+4 until end of turn.', "Bloodthirst 1 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nCreatures with power less than Skarrgan Pit-Skulk's power can't block it.", 'Bloodthirst 2 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nTrample', 'Bloodthirst 3 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nFlying\\n{R}{R}{R}: Return Skarrgan Firebird from your graveyard to your hand. Activate only if an opponent was dealt damage this turn.', 'Cackling Flames deals 3 damage to any target.\\nHellbent — Cackling Flames deals 5 damage instead if you have no cards in hand.', "Choose one —\\n• Creatures without flying can't block this turn.\\n• Gain control of all permanents you own.\\n• Gruul Charm deals 3 damage to each creature with flying.", "Choose one —\\n• Creatures you control gain lifelink until end of turn.\\n• Draw a card.\\n• Put target attacking or blocking creature on top of its owner's library.", "Choose one —\\n• Exile target player's graveyard.\\n• Destroy target artifact.\\n• Each creature deals 1 damage to its controller.", "Choose one —\\n• Return target creature you control and all Auras you control attached to it to their owner's hand.\\n• Destroy target creature and you lose life equal to its toughness.\\n• Return target creature card with mana value 1 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.", "Counter target spell, activated ability, or triggered ability. (Mana abilities can't be targeted.)", "Counter target spell. Its controller can't cast spells this turn.", 'Create an X/X green Ooze creature token, where X is the greatest power among creatures you control.', 'Deathtouch\\nBloodrush — {G}, Discard Wasteland Viper: Target attacking creature gets +1/+2 and gains deathtouch until end of turn.', "Deathtouch\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nFlying\\nWhen Stoic Ephemera blocks, sacrifice it at end of combat.", 'Defender, flying', "Demonfire deals X damage to any target. If a creature dealt damage this way would die this turn, exile it instead.\\nHellbent — If you have no cards in hand, this spell can't be countered and the damage can't be prevented.", 'Destroy target creature or land.', 'Destroy target creature or planeswalker.', "Destroy target creature. It can't be regenerated. That creature's controller creates a 3/3 green Frog Lizard creature token.", 'Destroy target monocolored creature.', 'Double strike\\nSavageborn Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{1}{R/G}: Put a +1/+1 counter on Savageborn Hydra. Activate only as a sorcery.', 'Double strike\\nWhen Crypt Champion enters the battlefield, each player puts a creature card with mana value 3 or less from their graveyard onto the battlefield.\\nWhen Crypt Champion enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless {R} was spent to cast it.', 'Draw three cards. You may play an additional land this turn.', "Elusive Krasis can't be blocked.\\nEvolve (Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, if that creature has greater power or toughness than this creature, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.)", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block, and its activated abilities can't be activated.\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature's controller, that player loses 1 life.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can\'t attack or block.\\nEnchanted creature has "At the beginning of your upkeep, you lose 1 life."', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -2/-2.\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature's controller, that player loses 2 life.", 'Enchant green creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +6/+6.\\n{G}{G}{G}, Sacrifice Wurmweaver Coil: Create a 6/6 green Wurm creature token.', 'Evolve (Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, if that creature has greater power or toughness than this creature, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.)\\nRemove two +1/+1 counters from Experiment One: Regenerate Experiment One. (The next time this creature would be destroyed, instead tap it, remove it from combat, and heal all damage on it.)', 'Evolve (Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, if that creature has greater power or toughness than this creature, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.)\\nWhenever a +1/+1 counter is put on Fathom Mage, you may draw a card.', 'Evolve (Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, if that creature has greater power or toughness than this creature, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.)\\n{T}: Add {G} for each +1/+1 counter on Gyre Sage.', 'Experiment Kraj has all activated abilities of each other creature with a +1/+1 counter on it.\\n{T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', 'Extort (Whenever you cast a spell, you may pay {W/B}. If you do, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain that much life.)\\nOther creatures you control have extort. (If a creature has multiple instances of extort, each triggers separately.)', 'Extort (Whenever you cast a spell, you may pay {W/B}. If you do, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain that much life.)\\nWhenever Treasury Thrull attacks, you may return target artifact, creature, or enchantment card from your graveyard to your hand.', "First strike, deathtouch\\nMaster of Cruelties can only attack alone.\\nWhenever Master of Cruelties attacks a player and isn't blocked, that player's life total becomes 1. Master of Cruelties assigns no combat damage this combat.", "First strike, haste\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", "First strike\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", "Flying, trample\\nShroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'Flying, trample\\nWhenever Rakdos the Defiler attacks, sacrifice half the non-Demon permanents you control, rounded up.\\nWhenever Rakdos deals combat damage to a player, that player sacrifices half the non-Demon permanents they control, rounded up.', 'Flying\\nEvolve (Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, if that creature has greater power or toughness than this creature, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.)', 'Flying\\nHaunt (When this creature dies, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen Belfry Spirit enters the battlefield or the creature it haunts dies, create two 1/1 black Bat creature tokens with flying.', 'Flying\\nNimbus Swimmer enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.', 'Flying\\nPride of the Clouds gets +1/+1 for each other creature with flying on the battlefield.\\nForecast — {2}{W}{U}, Reveal Pride of the Clouds from your hand: Create a 1/1 white and blue Bird creature token with flying. (Activate only during your upkeep and only once each turn.)', "Flying\\nSacrifice Judge's Familiar: Counter target instant or sorcery spell unless its controller pays {1}.", 'Flying\\nWhen Angel of Despair enters the battlefield, destroy target permanent.', 'Flying\\nWhen Deathpact Angel dies, create a 1/1 white and black Cleric creature token. It has "{3}{W}{B}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice this creature: Return a card named Deathpact Angel from your graveyard to the battlefield."', 'Flying\\nWhen Keening Banshee enters the battlefield, target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.', "Flying\\nWhen Lyev Skyknight enters the battlefield, detain target nonland permanent an opponent controls. (Until your next turn, that permanent can't attack or block and its activated abilities can't be activated.)", 'Flying\\nWhen Skeletal Vampire enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 black Bat creature tokens with flying.\\n{3}{B}{B}, Sacrifice a Bat: Create two 1/1 black Bat creature tokens with flying.\\nSacrifice a Bat: Regenerate Skeletal Vampire.', 'Flying\\nWhen Sky Hussar enters the battlefield, untap all creatures you control.\\nForecast — Tap two untapped white and/or blue creatures you control, Reveal Sky Hussar from your hand: Draw a card. (Activate only during your upkeep and only once each turn.)', "Flying\\nWhenever Archon of the Triumvirate attacks, detain up to two target nonland permanents your opponents control. (Until your next turn, those permanents can't attack or block and their activated abilities can't be activated.)", 'Flying\\nWhenever Isperia the Inscrutable deals combat damage to a player, choose a card name. That player reveals their hand. If a card with the chosen name is revealed this way, search your library for a creature card with flying, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "Flying\\nWhenever Skymark Roc attacks, you may return target creature defending player controls with toughness 2 or less to its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nWhenever Trygon Predator deals combat damage to a player, you may destroy target artifact or enchantment that player controls.', 'Flying\\nWhenever a Dragon you control attacks, create a 6/6 red Dragon creature token with flying.', 'Flying\\nWhenever a creature attacks you or a planeswalker you control, you may draw a card.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', "Flying\\n{W}: Windreaver gains vigilance until end of turn.\\n{W}: Windreaver gets +0/+1 until end of turn.\\n{U}: Switch Windreaver's power and toughness until end of turn.\\n{U}: Return Windreaver to its owner's hand.", "Graft 3 (This creature enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it. Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, you may move a +1/+1 counter from this creature onto it.)\\n{2}: Target creature with a +1/+1 counter on it gains shroud until end of turn. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'Graft 4 (This creature enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it. Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, you may move a +1/+1 counter from this creature onto it.)\\nWhen Cytoplast Root-Kin enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each other creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it.\\n{2}: Move a +1/+1 counter from target creature you control onto Cytoplast Root-Kin.', "Gruul Turf enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Gruul Turf enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {R}{G}.", 'Haste', "Haunt (When this creature dies, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen Orzhov Pontiff enters the battlefield or the creature it haunts dies, choose one —\\n• Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.\\n• Creatures you don't control get -1/-1 until end of turn.", 'Landfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on Vinelasher Kudzu.', "Orzhov Basilica enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Orzhov Basilica enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {W}{B}.", "Protection from red\\nWhen Lavinia of the Tenth enters the battlefield, detain each nonland permanent your opponents control with mana value 4 or less. (Until your next turn, those permanents can't attack or block and their activated abilities can't be activated.)", "Rakdos Carnarium enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Rakdos Carnarium enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {B}{R}.", "Rakdos's Return deals X damage to target opponent or planeswalker. That player or that planeswalker's controller discards X cards.", "Return target creature to its owner's hand. You gain 2 life.", "Rubblehulk's power and toughness are each equal to the number of lands you control.\\nBloodrush — {1}{R}{G}, Discard Rubblehulk: Target attacking creature gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the number of lands you control.", 'Sacrifice three white creatures: Exile target creature.\\nWhenever another black creature you control dies, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'Savage Twister deals X damage to each creature.', "Simic Growth Chamber enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Simic Growth Chamber enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {G}{U}.", 'Target creature gets +4/-4 until end of turn.', 'Target creature you control fights another target creature. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)', 'Trample\\nBloodrush — {R}{G}, Discard Ghor-Clan Rampager: Target attacking creature gets +4/+4 and gains trample until end of turn.', 'Trample\\nWhenever Borborygmos deals combat damage to a player, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.', 'Ulasht, the Hate Seed enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each other red creature you control and a +1/+1 counter on it for each other green creature you control.\\n{1}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Ulasht: Choose one —\\n• Ulasht deals 1 damage to target creature.\\n• Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', "Unleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Vigilance, reach\\nRuric Thar, the Unbowed attacks each combat if able.\\nWhenever a player casts a noncreature spell, Ruric Thar deals 6 damage to that player.', 'Vigilance\\nWhen Court Hussar enters the battlefield, look at the top three cards of your library, then put one of them into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.\\nWhen Court Hussar enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless {W} was spent to cast it.', "When Azorius Justiciar enters the battlefield, detain up to two target creatures your opponents control. (Until your next turn, those creatures can't attack or block and their activated abilities can't be activated.)", 'When Burning-Tree Emissary enters the battlefield, add {R}{G}.', "When Coiling Oracle enters the battlefield, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a land card, put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, put that card into your hand.", "When Detention Sphere enters the battlefield, you may exile target nonland permanent not named Detention Sphere and all other permanents with the same name as that permanent.\\nWhen Detention Sphere leaves the battlefield, return the exiled cards to the battlefield under their owner's control.", "When Ghost Council of Orzhova enters the battlefield, target opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.\\n{1}, Sacrifice a creature: Exile Ghost Council of Orzhova. Return it to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", 'When Protean Hulk dies, search your library for any number of creature cards with total mana value 6 or less, put them onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'When Sin Collector enters the battlefield, target opponent reveals their hand. You choose an instant or sorcery card from it and exile that card.', 'When Zegana, Utopian Speaker enters the battlefield, if you control another creature with a +1/+1 counter on it, draw a card.\\n{4}{G}{U}: Adapt 4. (If this creature has no +1/+1 counters on it, put four +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has trample.', 'Whenever Jagged Poppet is dealt damage, discard that many cards.\\nHellbent — Whenever Jagged Poppet deals combat damage to a player, if you have no cards in hand, that player discards cards equal to the damage.', 'Whenever Rubblebelt Raiders attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on it for each attacking creature you control.', "Whenever a player activates an ability that isn't a mana ability, Burning-Tree Shaman deals 1 damage to that player.", "Whenever you cast a green creature spell, you may search your library for a creature card, reveal it, then shuffle and put that card on top.\\nWhenever you cast a blue creature spell, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a creature card, put that card into your hand.", "You can't cast this spell unless an opponent lost life this turn.\\nFlying, trample\\nCreature spells you cast cost {1} less to cast for each 1 life your opponents have lost this turn.", 'You gain X life and draw X cards.', 'You may have Progenitor Mimic enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except it has "At the beginning of your upkeep, if this creature isn\'t a token, create a token that\'s a copy of this creature."', '{1}, {T}: Add {B}{R}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{U}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {R}{G}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{B}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{U}.', '{1}{W}{B}: Target creature gains lifelink until end of turn.\\n{1}{W}{B}: Whenever you gain life this turn, each opponent loses that much life.', '{2}, Sacrifice a creature: Lyzolda, the Blood Witch deals 2 damage to any target if the sacrificed creature was red. Draw a card if the sacrificed creature was black.', "{2}{W}: Tap target creature.\\n{2}{U}: Counter target activated ability. (Mana abilities can't be targeted.)", '{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', '{G}{U}, {T}: Double the number of each kind of counter on target artifact, creature, or land.', '{G}{U}: This turn, each creature you control enters the battlefield with an additional +1/+1 counter on it.\\n{G}{U}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from a creature you control: Draw a card.', '{R}{R}: Rakdos Pit Dragon gains flying until end of turn.\\n{R}: Rakdos Pit Dragon gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nHellbent — Rakdos Pit Dragon has double strike as long as you have no cards in hand.', '{T}: Add {B} or {R}.\\n{B}{R}: Rakdos Keyrune becomes a 3/1 black and red Devil artifact creature with first strike until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {G}.\\nWhenever you tap Zhur-Taa Druid for mana, it deals 1 damage to each opponent.', '{T}: Add {W} or {U}.\\n{W}{U}: Azorius Keyrune becomes a 2/2 white and blue Bird artifact creature with flying until end of turn.', '{T}: Target creature becomes a Frog with base power and toughness 3/3 until end of turn.', "{W}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature can't attack this turn."]
flavor: ['"All the coins in Ravnica can\'t save his soul now."\\n—Narbulg Nine Fingers', '"As peace should be—gentle yet unstoppable."\\n—Augustin IV', '"Finally, a weapon the Boros can\'t confiscate!"\\n—Juri, proprietor of the Juri Revue', '"I feel in them a sense of duty and commitment, yet I can feel nothing else. It is as if their duty is to an empty void."\\n—Razia', '"I like a little entertainment with my dinner."\\n—Rakdos', '"I never thought I\'d be so glad to see two tons of beak and claws bearing down on me at the speed of an arrow."\\n—Mirela, Azorius hussar', '"I serve only justice. But through that duty, I serve all of Ravnica."', '"I used to hurl rocks and eat scraps of meat burned over a fire. Look at what I\'ve become and tell me Simic does not hold infinite possibility."', '"If there were such a thing as a soul, I think it would be behind the gallbladder but above the kidneys."', '"It is technically an ooze, but its life span measures only seconds. In that short time, its appetite for magic is extraordinary."\\n—Simic research notes', '"It misses nothing and it has no sense of humor."\\n—Barvisa, courtroom scribe', '"It\'s easy to see why those Gruul dirtbags follow him—the only orders he gives are \'Crush them!\' and \'We eat!\'"\\n—Teysa Karlov', '"Let him be an example to others who would default on their debts to us."\\n—"The Cozen," Orzhov assassin', '"Let the knowledge of absolute law inspire you to live a life of absolute order."', '"Life is fleeting, and so is death. Only the oath is eternal."', '"Look at her, once filled with innocence. Death has a way of wringing away such . . . deficiencies."\\n—Savra', '"Meat *and* eggs. We eat!"\\n—Borborygmos', '"Nature is the ultimate mindless destroyer, capable of power and ferocity no army can match, and the Gruul follow its example."\\n—Trigori, Azorius senator', '"Not Gruul? Then die!"\\n—Borborygmos', '"Of course it will grow beyond control—it was designed to choose its own evolution."\\n—Momir Vig', '"Only the decadent think magic should be pristine and without cost."', '"Spend your life betraying me if you wish. I\'ll simply take it up with your ghost."', '"That must weigh heavily on your soul. Let me purge it for you."', '"The Gruul embrace all things poisonous and living in the cracks of society."\\n—Teysa Karlov', '"The Simic come from the cold slow depths. How could they understand the fire in a wild heart?"\\n—Kroshkar, Gruul shaman', '"The higher the mind soars, the greater its understanding of the law."\\n—Isperia', '"This city will perish, and the Gruul will cheer as the boar-god crushes the last bricks into dust."\\n—Nikya of the Old Ways', '"This creature has hyperevolved chameleonic abilities. It no longer mimics its surroundings, instead forcing them to take on its form."\\n—Simic research notes', '"Try not to look guilty. Or delicious."\\n—Thorpe, street urchin', '"We have confiscated your spells as evidence. Once we conclude our investigation, you may petition to have them returned."', '"We paid the Simic very well for this capability, but we should quickly recoup our expenses in saved wages."\\n—Milana, Orzhov prelate', '"We respect all lifeforms, but this one we respect from a distance."\\n—Mandor, Selesnya ranger', '"We\'ve bred out the shortcomings of the species\' natural form and replaced them with assets of our own design."\\n—Momir Vig', '"We\'ve merged your life essence with that of several creatures at once. You\'re welcome."\\n—Speaker Trifon', '"Your potential to commit a crime warrants further investigation."', 'As the Simic released more of their krasis experiments, they required new habitats, always at the expense of the locals.', 'As the bounty on Massacre Girl rose, so did the number of imitators.', 'As whispers and rumors increased, so did the demand for fail-safe barriers.', 'Devil-blades and dripping blood make music Rakdos never tires of hearing.', 'Few puppets are so willing.', 'For the Simic Combine, its sigil serves not as an emblem of honor but as a trademark. Its familiar image on any biological commodity attests to superb craftsmanship, ingenious innovation, and higher cost.', 'Gruul shamans are bent on punishing the civilized. Any act more complex than rubbing sticks together or eating with utensils is met with the stinging burn of their magic.', 'Gruul territorial markings need not be legible. The blood, snot, and muck used to smear them are unmistakably Gruul.', "Gurley was the first to domesticate one, though his widow didn't take much solace in that accomplishment.", 'Held aloft by metabolized magic, trygons are ravenous for sources of mystic fuel.', 'Her cold wail echoes in the alleys and under-eaves, finding the unfortunate and turning their blood to ice.', 'In Rakdos-controlled neighborhoods, everyone is part of the show.', 'It grows to hate you.', 'Its favorite treats are candied hands and sweet hearts.', "Long ago, birds of paradise littered the skies. Thanks to the city's sprawl, most now exist as pets of society's elite.", 'Made of bone and boiled in blood, a Rakdos signet is not considered finished until it has been used as a murder weapon.', 'Most auramancers would have let the spikes hover just above the skin. Having the spikes rip through the skin from beneath was a touch added by Rakdos himself.', 'One moment, conscious only of a sense of repose. The next moment, hearing the trudge of his own footsteps. He sighed and squinted into the glare ahead.', 'Rakdos cultists hanged her for sport in the township square. Her ghost now stands vigil at what has become known as the Tree of Weeping.', 'Rakdos festivals almost leave enough rubble in their wake to hide the bodies.', 'Sacrificial rites take place before an audience of cheering cultists, each begging to be the next on stage.', 'Snaking remnants of nature directed by a body of thought and progress, the oracles embody all that is Simic.', 'Some use magic to spy through walls. Others use it to crush them.', 'Such is the power of Rakdos that even his shadow takes on a cruel life of its own.', 'The Orzhov contract the Izzet to animate slum districts and banish them to the wastes. The Gruul adopt them and send them back to the city for vengeance.', 'The Rakdos use it for everything you can think of and plenty more than that.', 'The Simic soon discovered that the sky offered as few constraints on size as the sea.', 'The fear of dragons is as old and as powerful as the fear of death itself.', "The form of the sigil is just as important as the sigil itself. If it's carried on a medallion, its bearer is a master. If it's tattooed on the body, its bearer is a slave.", "The mask isn't meant to hide his identity. It's meant to keep the viscera out of his eyes.", 'The maze-like design embodies the core of Azorius law—strict structure designed to test wills and stall change.', 'They inflict pain to forget their own and break foes to feel whole.', 'Those who regard the Gruul as savage simpletons underestimate the subtle power of their shamans.', "When Lord Rakdos stirred from his slumber, everyone else's nightmare began.", 'Which is worse—the sleep which never ends or that which never comes?']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Alayna Danner', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Charles Urbach', 'Chase Stone', 'Chippy', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Daren Bader', 'David Rapoza', 'Dimitar Marinski', 'Efrem Palacios', 'Ekaterina Burmak', 'Eytan Zana', 'Greg Staples', 'Howard Lyon', 'Izzy', 'Jack Wang', 'James Paick', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Chan', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Johannes Voss', 'John Avon', 'Justin Sweet', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Liam Sharp', 'Luca Zontini', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Marc Simonetti', 'Marcelo Vignali', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Winters', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Mike Bierek', 'Mike Sass', 'Mitch Cotie', 'Nottsuo', 'Pat Lee', 'Pete Venters', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Ravenna Tran', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Robert Bliss', 'Ron Spears', 'Ryan Barger', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Sara Winters', 'Scott Chou', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Shishizaru', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Victor Adame Minguez', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Wesley Burt', 'Willian Murai', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Yigit Koroglu', 'Zoltan Boros', 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai', 'rk post']
